      trivia: "Crowned Heads' marque names are almost all made of coded references to culture. Jericho Hill is Johnny Cash's live album; Headley Grange, the place where Led Zeppelin recorded; Four Kicks, a Kings of Leon song; J.D. Howard, Jesse James's alias; Le Carême, the legendary French chef — music, history, art and cuisine woven together. The company name itself is credited to the sign on the wagon in The Wizard of Oz, and Nashville's musical culture and love of popular culture breathe through the naming at every turn."
